mindmap
root((contributing to this plugin))
  decide which of the two you have
    a claim about a method
      you have a source and it says the check should work differently
      you found a defect in how a judgement is computed
    a claim about behaviour
      a tool answered something you believe is wrong
      a tool refused, crashed, or took the process down
    if it is both, file the behaviour first
      a method proposal is easier to judge once the behaviour is agreed
  an improvement with a source
    what you must cite
      the published method, with its year and venue
      the house convention it would replace
        provenance tables separate the two
          4 of 10 reference files carry one today
        most of the shipped checks are house conventions
    what you must say about the judgement
      which check changes, by its code
        codes are declared across 14 source files
        the 75 in engine are the largest group
      whether it changes a verdict or adds a signal
        only violation level decides a verdict
      what it does NOT decide, in words
    what it must come with
      the nearest case that must still pass
        a check that fires on everything proves nothing
      a mutation that makes the new case go red
        a case that cannot fail is not a case
      the far side of the tradeoff, if there is one
        a method that buys precision with runtime needs saying
  a problem you hit while running it
    what to send
      the exact call, with its arguments
        the tool name and the full arguments object
      what you got
        the verdict and the verdict reason
        the finding codes, verbatim
        the schema, since the reading order differs by family
      what you expected instead, and why
        the rule or the source that says so
    the shapes worth reporting first
      a verdict that reads as a pass over nothing
        a check that never ran is not a check that passed
      a refusal where a report was expected
      a raw error with no code to route on
      the process dying or the search not stopping
    what makes it reproducible
      the smallest model or diagram that shows it
        strip it until removing anything makes the effect go away
      the version, and the schema you got
      whether it is stable or intermittent
        a report is deterministic by contract, so say which
  what both have to pass
    the gates, in the order CI runs them
      Node 20, 22
      typecheck
      build
      the regression chain
      the committed build must match the source
        the build output is committed, so it moves with the change
    the house rules a suite follows
      one code per case, no other error beside it
      assert which check carries the finding
      every code gets a near miss that must not fire
      an unreachable code is pinned, not skipped
      no brittle counts, in text or in a test name
    the documents that must move with the change
      the reference file for the domain
      the memory entry, when a decision was made
      the bilingual pair together
